# Credential store

How this process stores and loads secrets when it holds them.

## Hard rules

1. Never log private keys, cert PEMs, tokens, or join material — even partially.
2. Prefer OS/keychain/TPM-backed storage when available; degraded file storage
   requires an ADR with expiry (**`rust-device-adr.mdc`**).
3. **Whether this process is the only holder of device-root identity** is
   product topology — consumer ADR — not constitution exclusivity law.

